    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said, “Good. I will make a treaty with you, but one thing I require of you. That is, you will not see my face unless you first bring Michal, Saul’s daughter, when you come to see my face.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "David sent messengers to Ishbosheth, Saul’s son, saying, “Deliver me my wife Michal, whom I was given to marry for one hundred foreskins of the Philistines.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA6:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "As the LORD’s ark came into David’s city, Michal the daughter of Saul looked out through the window and saw King David leaping and dancing before the LORD; and she despised him in her heart."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA6:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then David returned to bless his household. Michal the daughter of Saul came out to meet David, and said, “How glorious the king of Israel was today, who uncovered himself today in the eyes of his servants’ maids, as one of the vain fellows shamelessly uncovers himself!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA6:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said to Michal, “It was before the LORD, who chose me above your father, and above all his house, to appoint me prince over the people of the LORD, over Israel. Therefore I will celebrate before the LORD."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA6:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "Michal the daughter of Saul had no child to the day of her death."
      }
    ],
